.\" jb.1 — manual page for jb
.\"
.TH JB 1 "May 24, 2025" "jb 0.1" "General Commands Manual"
.
.SH NAME
jb \- a minimal agentic coding loop
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo
.I prompt
|
.BR jb
.br
.B jb
.B \-\-parent
.I uuid
.br
.B jb
.B \-\-version
.br
.B jb
.B \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B jb
utility reads a prompt from standard input, sends it to a language model
API, executes any tool calls the model requests in a loop, and prints the
final answer to standard output.
.PP
.B jb
is a filter: stdin is the prompt, stdout is the answer.  There are no
command-line arguments beyond
.B \-\-version
and
.BR \-\-help .
Behavior is determined entirely by the configuration file, the working
directory, and the filesystem.
.PP
The
.B \-\-parent
flag records a parent session UUID in the session metadata,
creating a session tree for observability.  It is typically
auto-injected by the
.B jb
tool and not used directly.
.
.SS The Agentic Loop
Each
.I turn
consists of sending the full conversation to the API, receiving a
streaming response, and acting on it:
.IP \(bu 3
If the model requests tool calls,
.B jb
executes them and feeds the results back, then starts another turn.
.IP \(bu 3
If the model emits a final text message
.RI ( finish_reason "stop"),
.B jb
prints it to stdout and exits.
.IP \(bu 3
If a configurable token budget is exhausted, the partial answer is
printed and the process exits with code 2.
.
.SS Tools
The model has access to five tools:
.TP
.BR read " \fIpath\fR [offset=\fIN\fR] [limit=\fIN\fR]"
Read file contents with line numbers.  Supports offset and limit for
large files.
.TP
.BR write " \fIpath\fR \fIcontent\fR"
Create or overwrite a file.  Creates parent directories as needed.
.TP
.BR edit " \fIpath\fR edits=[{oldText,newText},...]"
Make precise text replacements in a file.  Each edit must match a unique,
non-overlapping region.  Multiple disjoint edits can be applied in a
single call.
.TP
.BR bash " \fIcommand\fR [timeout=\fIN\fR]"
Execute a shell command.  The model decides the timeout per command.
If omitted, the command runs to completion.
.PP
.TP
.BR jb " \fIprompt\fR [timeout=\fIN\fR]"
Spawn a child
.B jb
session to delegate a task.  The child runs independently
and returns its final answer via stdout.  The parent session
UUID is automatically injected \(em the model does not see it.
The child's metadata records the parent, forming a session tree.
.PP
A sub-agent is a child
.B jb
process spawned via the
.B jb
tool.  It has its own session, its own API calls, and returns its
answer via stdout.  The child starts with a fresh context \(em
it does not inherit the parent's conversation.
.
.SS Session Model
Each run creates a session directory under
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jb/sessions/<uuid>/ ,
containing:
.TP
.B state.jsonl
Append-only JSONL.  One message per line.  The full conversation.
.TP
.B log.jsonl
Real-time log of raw SSE events.  Use
.B tail -f
to watch the agent work.
.PP
The full message array is sent to the API every turn.  The API is
stateless.
.
.SS Skills
A
.I skill
is a directory containing a
.B SKILL.md
file with YAML frontmatter
.RI ( name ","
description ) and a markdown body.
Skills are discovered from:
.IP \(bu 3
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jb/agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
\(em global skills
.IP \(bu 3
.B .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
\(em project-local skills
.PP
An index of available skills is injected into the system prompt.
The model reads the full
.B SKILL.md
on demand via the
.B read
tool.
.
.SS Project Context
.B AGENTS.md
files are discovered by walking from the current working directory
upward to the root.  Their contents are concatenated (root first) and
appended to the system prompt unconditionally.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B jb
reads its configuration from
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jb/config.json .
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
    "api_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
    "model": "gpt-4.1",
    "max_tokens": 500000,
    "max_output_lines": 2000,
    "max_output_bytes": 51200
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
All fields are optional.  Defaults are shown above.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JB_API_KEY
API key for the language model endpoint.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Fallback API key if
.B JB_API_KEY
is not set.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration directory.  Defaults to
.BR $HOME/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Cache directory for session data.  Defaults to
.BR $HOME/.cache .
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory for temporary files (bash output exceeding limits).
Defaults to
.BR /tmp .
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jb/config.json
Configuration file.
.TP
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jb/sessions/<uuid>/state.jsonl
Session state \(em the full conversation as JSONL.
.TP
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jb/sessions/<uuid>/log.jsonl
Session log \(em raw SSE events for observability.
.TP
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jb/sessions/<uuid>/metadata.json
Session metadata \(em status, title, timing, model, and optional parent UUID.
.TP
.B AGENTS.md
Project context file.  Walked from cwd upward.
.TP
.B .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
Project-local skill definitions.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.  Final answer printed to stdout.
.TP
.B 1
API or model error after retries.
.TP
.B 2
Token budget exhausted or tool execution error.
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error (missing API key, malformed config, no prompt on stdin).
.TP
.B 130
Process killed by SIGINT.
.TP
.B 143
Process killed by SIGTERM.
.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT
Kill child processes, write final state to log, print partial answer
to stdout, exit 130.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Same as SIGINT, exit 143.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Default disposition (die).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read a file and ask about it:
.RS
.B cat main.c | jb
.RE
.PP
Inline prompt:
.RS
.B jb <<< "list files in the current directory"
.RE
.PP
Pipe a specification:
.RS
.B cat spec.md | jb
.RE
.PP
Print version:
.RS
.B jb --version
.RE
.PP
Read this manual page from within a jb session:
.RS
.B man jb | col -b
.RE
.
.SH BUGS
.B jb
has no known bugs.  See session log for details.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR col (1)
